<title>PHILIPPINES: Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly lower.</title>
<headline>Manila's PHIBOR rates mostly lower.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Philippine interbank offered rates (PHIBOR) were mostly lower on Thursday in step with the high liquidity in the system, traders said.</p>
<p>Among the various terms, the one- and two-month rates were steady.</p>
<p>Dealers said the system had been swamped with more peso liquidity after it was injected with the proceeds of a Europeso issuance.  </p>
<p>Average rates quoted by 20 banks were:</p>
<p>			 MARCH 13		 MARCH 12</p>
<p>    1 W		9  1/4		  9  5/16</p>
<p>    2 W		9  1/4		  9  5/16</p>
<p>    1 M		9  5/16		 9  5/16</p>
<p>    2 M		9  1/2		  9  1/2</p>
<p>    3 M		9  1/2		  9  5/8</p>
<p>    6 M		9  3/4		  9  7/8</p>
<p>    12M		10			10  1/8</p>
<p>    VAL		14-Mar		  13-Mar</p>
<p>--LILIAN KARUNUNGAN (632) 841-8937</p>
</text>
